SD>Polymorph traps are one of the least understood elements of Nethack, for
SD>some reason. If you step on a polymorph trap, you polymorph and the trap
SD>disappears. 

    One exception: If you are magic protected, you will not polymorph while
stepping on a polymorph trap, nor will you make it disappear.  Between certain
advantages gained while polymorphed into some creatures (like the unlabelled
but extremely useful "flying" intrinsic which has all the advantages and 
none of the disadvantages of levitation, and the "extra" hit points and 
attacks) and fear of random polymorph, I typically, when I get my WoW, make
sure I have magic resistance, polymorph control, and the ability to polymorph.

